[[1257,496,"The availability and use of illicit drugs posed a threat to the stability of the prison, contributing to debt, bullying and fear. The positive drug testing rate at HMP High Down was among the highest in adult male prisons","illicit drug availability",""],[1258,496,"The availability of illicit substances continued to be a serious concern that undermined safety and stability. The rate of positive drug tests remained as high as at our full inspection in 2023","illicit substance availability",""],[1259,496,"It's probably easier to get [REDACTED] or a mobile phone in here than it is to get sugar. I think some prisoners may get coerced and groomed into taking it and running up debts","coerced drug use",""],[1260,496,"[REDACTED] is a daily occurrence, it's too much to handle...some batches are bad and they can then be violent","daily drug exposure",""],[1261,496,"nearly every day when someone is found under the influence of NPS (New psychoactive substances)","NPS exposure",""],[1262,496,"If they have access to a phone it makes it easier for them to obtain drugs","mobile phone access",""],[1263,496,"prisoners were able to get possession of smart phones (even though they are not allowed to have them), and that having access to smart phones enabled prisoners to arrange for contraband to be delivered into prison, threaten and coerce, communicate across different prisons, and take and share video footage within the prison","smartphone-enabled contraband",""],[1264,496,"[REDACTED] defence technology exists to detect, track [REDACTED] and identify","detection technology",""],[1265,496,"The Office of National Statistics recorded, however, that between 2008 and 2019 there were 145 drug-related deaths in UK prisons, which equates to an average of 13.2 pa over that 11-year period","drug-related mortality",""],[1266,496,"The 6th Report of the House of Commons Justice Committee states that between December 2022 and December 2024 there were 136 drug-related deaths in UK prisons, which equates to 68 death per year in that 2-year period, in other words about one every 5 days","drug-related mortality",""],[1267,496,"(1) New psychoactive substances, especially [REDACTED] , are easily available in HM Prison High Down, as in many other prisons in England & Wales","NPS availability",""],[1268,496,"(2) Mobile phones are easily available in HM Prison High Down, as in many other prisons in England & Wales","mobile phone availability",""],[14666,5734,"The proper and regular monitoring of all medication that is prescribed by way of a repeat prescription","lack of proper and regular monitoring of repeat prescribed medication",""],[14667,5734,"The preparation of structured care plans for each patient","absence of structured care plans",""],[14668,5734,"An effective procedure for following up patients who fail to attend pre-‐‐booked appointments with clinicians","no follow‑up for missed appointments",""],[14669,5734,"The effective use of Read Codes on the System One record, to flag up and highlight significant risk factors in a patient's care","ineffective use of Read Codes to flag risk factors",""],[14670,5734,"Ensuring that all staff with responsibility for patients in prison have received adequate foundation training and on-‐‐going training in the ACCT procedure","inadequate training of staff in ACCT procedure",""],[14671,5734,"Ensuring that caseworkers are aware of and attend ACCT Case Reviews for patients under their care","caseworkers not attending ACCT Case Reviews",""]]